{"title":"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 35","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_35\">Problem 35</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 35\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rhombus is formed by two radii and two chords of a circle whose radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet. The area of the rhombus in square feet is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08455f68623c25e51936ee8c943d92b75c7ff80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 128\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 128\\sqrt{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 256\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 512\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 512\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"490\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fba1514e47c27c2da9987e41d4846d43581e117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 16\\text{ ft}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> be the radius of the circle.\n</p><p>The rhombus consists of two radii and two chords, so all four sides equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b49ee206ec8075679c1af16f97c1322b6cfe3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />. The diagonal connecting the center to the circle's edge is also a radius of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b49ee206ec8075679c1af16f97c1322b6cfe3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>This diagonal splits the rhombus into two congruent equilateral triangles with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e3ae8f743768f3362c1722a99f9ddcf3e156274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb36c24f177f8569ffc377419785b8481811130.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area} = 2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} (16)^2 = 128\\sqrt{3}\\text{ sq ft}\\]\" width=\"357\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>This corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b796948f763471dad529946914e565390e3b9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME\" title=\"1956 AHSME\">1956 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1956 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1956\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 34\">Problem 34</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 36\">Problem 36</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.ph